["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalRefType/securityOther", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalRefType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/FunctionalSafety/EvaluationResult", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "EvaluationResult represents the documented outcome of assessing a work product, like a requirement, system, component, or process against specified criteria. It records whether the evaluated subject has met, failed, or yielded an inconclusive result based on the applied EvaluationResultType. The EvaluationResult captures the rationale behind the conclusion, providing necessary context and justification while referencing the specific RequirementVerification upon which the evaluation was based. This structure ensures clear traceability and supports compliance with standards for rigorous verification and validation processes.\n\nAn EvaluationResult with an evaluation value of \"inconclusive\" should have a value in its comment property.\n\nA rationale is a detailed explanation or reasoning that supports the\nEvaluationResult. It provides the underlying justification for why\nan evaluation was deemed to have passed, failed, or been inconclusive.\nThis clarifies the decision-making process, citing evidence, criteria,\nanalysis methods, and any considerations of uncertainties or risks.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Software/homePage", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type", "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty", "globalId", "", ""]
["_:Ndf47f55ab2604b03a43c85454fb505c7", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#maxCount", "1", "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/headquartersLocation", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note", "Headquarters denotes the location where most or all of the important functions of an organization are coordinated. In the United States, the corporate headquarters represents the entity at the center or the top of a corporation taking full responsibility for managing all business activities.\nTo identify an organization's headquarters accurately, you provide address information (mailing, street and GPL) information related to the organization\u2019s headquarters.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["_:N52fb5fd7570f45c0960e97bfd6eeaa6e", "http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#path", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/relationshipType", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Dataset/hasSensitivePersonalInformation", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment", "Describes if any sensitive personal information is present in the dataset.", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/HashAlgorithm/sha224", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/hasVariant", "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy", "https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/", "globalId", "", ""]
["https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/ismn", "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition", "International Standard Music Number (ISMN) <https://ismn-international.org/ismn/the-ismn/> is a unique numeric identifier for printed music (notated music) standardized by ISO 10957 <https://www.iso.org/standard/83122.html>. It consists of either 10 characters (starting with the letter \"M\" for assignments prior to January 1, 2008) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISMN is composed of four parts: the GS1 prefix 979-0, a registrant element, an item element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., 9790006538424).", "http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#langString", "en", ""]
